# ─── CloudOps Portfolio — environment ────────────────────────────────────────
#
# THE PORTFOLIO BUILD NEEDS NONE OF THESE TO RUN.
#
# Every value that used to point at a real backend is now served by the mock
# data layer (src/lib/mock/data.ts). The console, service map, traces, metrics,
# and load generator all animate with synthetic data out of the box. Just run
# `npm install && npm run dev` — no .env required.
#
# The variables below are documented only so you can see what the real CloudOps
# storefront wired up, and in case you later point this copy at a live backend.
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in ONLY if you deliberately want live data.

# ─── Observability backends (real app: in-cluster Tempo / Mimir / Loki) ───────
# Left unset here — the mock /api/observe/* routes ignore them entirely.
# TEMPO_URL=
# MIMIR_URL=
# LOKI_URL=

# ─── Storefront catalog / orders API (real app: order-api on EKS) ─────────────
# Only the unreachable cart/checkout/product routes referenced these. The
# portfolio nav never hits them.
# API_BASE_URL=
# SEARCH_BASE_URL=

# ─── Load generator (real app: internal loadgen service, HMAC-signed) ─────────
# The mock /api/load/* routes simulate a run in memory; these are unused.
# LOADGEN_URL=
# INTERNAL_HMAC_SECRET=

# ─── Cognito / OIDC auth (real app only) ──────────────────────────────────────
# The portfolio has no auth — every page is public. Setting these would only
# re-enable the /login redirect flow, which has no Cognito to talk to.
# OIDC_HOSTED_UI=
# OIDC_CLIENT_ID=
# OIDC_AUDIENCE=
# SESSION_JWT_SECRET=

# ─── Public build-time flags ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Set to "1" to surface the internal /design system-preview page + its nav link.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_DESIGN_PREVIEW=0
